WEBVTT

00:00.290 --> 00:02.410
- [Instructor] We're told that
Taylor opened a restaurant.

00:02.410 --> 00:05.050
The net value of the restaurant
in thousands of dollars,

00:05.050 --> 00:07.130
t months after its opening is modeled

00:07.130 --> 00:11.550
by v of t is equal to
two t squared minus 20t.

00:11.550 --> 00:12.520
Taylor wants to know

00:12.520 --> 00:16.640
what the restaurant's
lowest net value will be,

00:16.640 --> 00:21.640
underline that, and when
it will reach that value.

00:22.060 --> 00:24.190
So let's break it down step by step.

00:24.190 --> 00:26.240
The function which describes

00:26.240 --> 00:27.890
how the value of the restaurant,

00:27.890 --> 00:29.110
the net value of the restaurant,

00:29.110 --> 00:30.770
changes over time is right over here.

00:30.770 --> 00:33.130
If I were to graph it, I
can see that the coefficient

00:33.130 --> 00:35.030
on the quadratic term is positive,

00:35.030 --> 00:37.800
so it's going to be some form
of upward-opening parabola.

00:37.800 --> 00:39.320
I don't know exactly what it looks like,

00:39.320 --> 00:41.360
we can think about that in a second.

00:41.360 --> 00:44.830
And so it's going to have
some point, right over here,

00:44.830 --> 00:47.390
which really is the
vertex of this parabola,

00:47.390 --> 00:50.130
where it's going to hit
its lowest in that value,

00:50.130 --> 00:52.280
and that's going to happen at some time t,

00:52.280 --> 00:57.020
if you can imagine that this
right over here is the t-axis.

00:57.020 --> 01:00.390
So my first question
is, is there some form,

01:00.390 --> 01:02.050
is there some way that I can re-write

01:02.050 --> 01:05.030
this function algebraically
so it becomes very easy

01:05.030 --> 01:07.010
to pick out this low point,

01:07.010 --> 01:10.110
which is essentially the
vertex of this parabola?

01:10.110 --> 01:12.010
Pause this video and think about that.

01:13.310 --> 01:15.590
All right, so you can imagine the form

01:15.590 --> 01:17.820
that I'm talking about is vertex form,

01:17.820 --> 01:20.270
where you can clearly spot the vertex.

01:20.270 --> 01:21.620
And the way we can do that

01:21.620 --> 01:23.750
is actually by completing the square.

01:23.750 --> 01:25.810
So the first thing I will do is,

01:25.810 --> 01:27.390
actually let me factor out a two here,

01:27.390 --> 01:30.130
because two is a common
factor of both of these terms.

01:30.130 --> 01:35.010
So v of t would be equal to
two times t squared minus 10t.

01:35.010 --> 01:37.090
And I'm going to leave some space,

01:37.090 --> 01:41.330
because completing the square,
which gets us to vertex form,

01:41.330 --> 01:43.050
is all about adding and subtracting

01:43.050 --> 01:44.760
the same value on one side.

01:44.760 --> 01:47.160
So we're not actually changing
the value of that side,

01:47.160 --> 01:48.310
but writing it in a way

01:48.310 --> 01:51.430
so we have a perfect square expression,

01:51.430 --> 01:52.410
and then we're probably going

01:52.410 --> 01:55.110
to add or subtract some value out here.

01:55.110 --> 01:57.160
Now how do we make this a
perfect square expression?

01:57.160 --> 01:59.070
If any of this business

01:59.070 --> 02:01.100
about completing the square
looks unfamiliar to you,

02:01.100 --> 02:02.730
I encourage you to look
up completing the square

02:02.730 --> 02:04.530
on Khan Academy and review that.

02:04.530 --> 02:06.860
But the way that we complete the square

02:06.860 --> 02:10.560
is we look at this first degree
coefficient right over here,

02:10.560 --> 02:13.100
it's negative 10, and we say all right,

02:13.100 --> 02:15.680
well let's take half
of that and square it.

02:15.680 --> 02:19.490
So half of negative 10 is negative five,

02:19.490 --> 02:22.130
and if we were to square it, that's 25.

02:22.130 --> 02:24.960
So if we add 25 right over here,

02:24.960 --> 02:27.520
then this is going to become
a perfect square expression.

02:27.520 --> 02:29.890
And you can see that
it would be equivalent

02:29.890 --> 02:33.440
to this entire thing,
if we add 25 like that,

02:33.440 --> 02:38.440
is going to be equivalent
to t minus five squared,

02:38.470 --> 02:39.770
just this part right over here.

02:39.770 --> 02:43.580
That's why we took half
of this and we squared it.

02:43.580 --> 02:46.440
But as I alluded to a few seconds
ago, or a few minutes ago,

02:46.440 --> 02:50.269
you can't just willy
nilly add 25 to one side

02:50.269 --> 02:52.821
of an equation like this,

02:52.821 --> 02:55.960
that will make this
equality no longer true.

02:55.960 --> 02:58.590
And in fact we didn't just add 25.

02:58.590 --> 03:02.260
Remember we have this two out
here, we added two times 25.

03:02.260 --> 03:05.110
You can verify that if
you redistribute the two,

03:05.110 --> 03:09.590
you'd get two t squared minus 20t plus 50,

03:09.590 --> 03:11.550
plus two times 25.

03:11.550 --> 03:14.520
So in order to make the equality,

03:14.520 --> 03:17.360
or in order to allow it
to continue to be true,

03:17.360 --> 03:20.090
we have to subtract 50.

03:20.090 --> 03:20.970
So just to be clear,

03:20.970 --> 03:24.390
this isn't some kind of
strange thing I'm doing,

03:24.390 --> 03:27.370
all I did was add 50 and subtract 50.

03:27.370 --> 03:29.280
You're saying wait, you added 25, not 50.

03:29.280 --> 03:32.970
No look, when I added 25
here, it's in a parenthesis,

03:32.970 --> 03:35.980
and then the whole expression
is multiplied by two,

03:35.980 --> 03:39.670
so I really did add 50 here,
so then I subtract 50 here

03:39.670 --> 03:42.000
to get to what I originally had.

03:42.000 --> 03:43.840
And when you view it that way,

03:43.840 --> 03:48.840
now v of t is going to be equal
to two times this business,

03:49.150 --> 03:51.530
which we already established
is t minus five squared,

03:51.530 --> 03:55.860
and then we have the minus 50.

03:55.860 --> 03:57.440
Now why is this form useful?

03:57.440 --> 04:01.610
This is vertex form, it's very
easy to pick out the vertex.

04:01.610 --> 04:04.730
It's very easy to pick
out when the low point is.

04:04.730 --> 04:09.730
The low point here happens
when this part is minimized.

04:11.120 --> 04:12.620
And this part is
minimized, think about it,

04:12.620 --> 04:15.310
you have two times something squared.

04:15.310 --> 04:16.590
So if you have something squared,

04:16.590 --> 04:17.720
it's going to hit its lowest point

04:17.720 --> 04:20.330
when this something is zero,

04:20.330 --> 04:22.480
otherwise it's going
to be a positive value.

04:22.480 --> 04:25.440
And so this part right over here is going

04:25.440 --> 04:29.150
to be equal to zero
when t is equal to five.

04:29.150 --> 04:33.770
So the lowest value is
when t is equal to five.

04:33.770 --> 04:35.993
Let me do that in a different color,

04:35.993 --> 04:37.650
don't wanna reuse the colors too much.

04:37.650 --> 04:41.787
So if we say v of five

04:44.130 --> 04:45.810
is going to be equal

04:45.810 --> 04:50.810
to two times five minus five,

04:54.140 --> 04:55.450
trying to keep up with the colors,

04:55.450 --> 04:58.860
minus five squared minus 50.

04:58.860 --> 05:02.030
Notice this whole thing
becomes zero right over here.

05:02.030 --> 05:05.180
So v of five is equal to negative 50,

05:05.180 --> 05:06.710
that is when we hit our low point,

05:06.710 --> 05:09.490
in terms of the net
value of the restaurant.

05:09.490 --> 05:13.063
So t represents months,
so we hit our low point,

05:14.363 --> 05:17.150
we rewrote our function
in a form, in vertex form,

05:17.150 --> 05:18.440
so it's easy to pick out this value,

05:18.440 --> 05:21.860
and we see that this low point
happens at t equals five,

05:21.860 --> 05:24.460
which is at time five months.

05:24.460 --> 05:26.930
And then what is that lowest net value?

05:26.930 --> 05:28.020
Well it's negative 50.

05:28.020 --> 05:30.530
And remember, the function
gives us the net value

05:30.530 --> 05:34.843
in thousands of dollars,
so it's negative $50,000

05:36.280 --> 05:40.270
is the lowest net value of the restaurant.

05:40.270 --> 05:41.103
And you might say how do you

05:41.103 --> 05:43.440
have a negative value of something,

05:43.440 --> 05:46.630
well imagine if, say the
building is worth $50,000,

05:46.630 --> 05:49.333
but the restaurant owes $100,000,

05:49.333 --> 05:52.483
then it would have a
negative $50,000 net value.
